// once when a program calls `toFixed` and called by the code generator,
// after its check of `d` (0 to 100), in place of the runtime's
// `isc_to_fixed`. `d` decimals, the exact value of `x` rounded to the
// nearest, a half away from zero, the texts of `write_fixed` of the
// interpreter (D155, D487). A float below 2^52 is `m` / 2^`s`: its whole
// part, and for at most 18 decimals its fraction times 10^`d` in 128 bits,
// rounded (`$roundShift`), one more in the whole part when the fraction
// rounds to 1; the digits of both in words, laid out by `$fixedText`. The
// rest out of the way (`$fixedRest`, `@cold`): more decimals, the integers
// from 2^52 on, the numbers from 1e21 on, what is not a number.
function $rtFixedText(x: f64, d: i64): string {
